---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/site';
import { comparePostsDayOrder, isoDate } from '../../lib/posts';

const allPosts = await getCollection('posts');
const todayKey = isoDate(new Date());
const todaysPosts = allPosts
  .filter((post) => isoDate(post.data.pubDate) === todayKey)
  .sort(comparePostsDayOrder);
const todayHref =
  todaysPosts.length > 0
    ? withBase(`posts/${todaysPosts[0].slug}/`)
    : withBase();
const readingHref = withBase('readings/sermon-on-the-mount/');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Start here"
  description="Who Jesus is, in plain words — and three gentle next steps to begin walking with Him."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Start here</h1>
    <p>
      Jesus is the Son of God who came close to ordinary people. He healed, forgave,
      taught with authority and kindness, and gave His life so we could be brought home
      to God. He is alive. He still invites anyone who is curious, tired, or hurting:
      <em>Come and see.</em>
    </p>
    <p>
      You do not need to have everything figured out. A next step can be small.
    </p>

    <h2>Three next steps</h2>
    <ol class="start-steps">
      <li>
        <a href={withBase('learn/')}><strong>Learn</strong></a>
        — short lessons on who Jesus is, reading a Gospel, prayer, hard days, and walking with Him daily.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={withBase('hard-times/')}><strong>Hard times</strong></a>
        — if something hurts right now, begin with a short verse for that need.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={withBase('sit/')}><strong>Sit with Jesus</strong></a>
        — a quiet minute with today’s word before you do anything else.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={readingHref}><strong>A longer reading</strong></a>
        — sit slowly with Jesus’ own words in the Sermon on the Mount.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={todayHref}><strong>Today’s reflection</strong></a>
        — a quiet morning, midday, or evening word for this day.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      When you are ready for more:
      <a href={withBase()}>Home</a>,
      <a href={withBase('learn/')}>Learn</a>,
      <a href={withBase('pray/')}>Pray</a>,
      <a href={withBase('faq/')}>FAQ</a>,
      <a href={withBase('readings/')}>all readings</a>,
      <a href={withBase('about/')}>About</a>, or
      <a href={withBase('de/')}>Deutsch (Willkommen)</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
